            "modified": "2026-08-18T07:49:21.601318Z",
            "name": "Impair Defenses: Disable or Modify Tools",
            "description": "[confidence=medium, sources=static] The API functions OpenProcess, TerminateProcess, WTSEnumerateProcessesW are all imported by the binary. This is a coherent enumerate-then-kill primitive: deliberately searching the process list (WTSEnumerateProcessesW) rather than acting on a handle already held, then opening and terminating a match. Consistent with Impair Defenses: Disable or Modify Tools (T1562.001) even without a decrypted target name to confirm which process is targeted -- medium rather than high confidence for that reason.",
            "external_references": [
                {
                    "source_name": "mitre-attack",
                    "url": "https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1562/001/",
                    "external_id": "T1562.001"
